  "rationale": "The plant G models a mobile robot executing a square path in a grid world, with explicit states for each side/corner and recovery. It allows all perception and motion events, including obstacle and recovery behaviors. The specification E enforces safe obstacle handling, ensures move_backward is only used for front-obstacle recovery, and guarantees the robot resumes the square sequence after recovery. Only one controllable is enabled per state, and uncontrollable events are total. The design biases toward forward progress and square coverage, using conservative recovery only when needed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Explicitly encode square path progress with states for each side and corner, so the robot resumes the square after recovery.",
    "Obstacle recovery uses short directed turns; move_backward is only allowed after obstacle_front, and full_rotate is reserved for repeated failures. All uncontrollable events are total, and only one controllable is enabled per state."
  ],
